  <!-- ============ SECTION 29 ============ -->
  <div class="section-header" id="s29"><span class="num">29</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
  <div class="three-col">
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Realisationsprinzip</div><div class="glossary-def">The principle that profits are recognised only when realised as of the balance sheet date, never on unrealised gains.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Imparitätsprinzip</div><div class="glossary-def">The asymmetric principle requiring all foreseeable losses to be recognised immediately, even before they are realised.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Niederstwertprinzip</div><div class="glossary-def">The lower-of-cost-and-market principle, applied strictly (regardless of permanence) to current assets under §253(4).</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Wertaufholungsgebot</div><div class="glossary-def">The mandatory requirement to reverse a prior write-down once its underlying cause no longer exists, except for goodwill.</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="card cn">
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Bewertungseinheit</div><div class="glossary-def">A valuation unit combining a hedged item and hedging instrument, suspending individual valuation to the extent risks offset.</div></div>
      <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Herstellungskosten</div><div class="glossary-def">Production cost, with materials, labour, and production overheads forming a mandatory capitalisation floor since BilMoG 2009.</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

